# Changelog

## 1.3.0
Power upgrade: input protection, a protected 5 V rail and per-slot rail selection.

* VBUS input protection at the USB-C connector: resettable polyfuse **F1**
  (MF-MSMF110/16-2, 1.1 A hold / 16 V) in series with VBUS and TVS **D2**
  (SMAJ5.0A) on the protected node, both upstream of FB1.
* New protected **5V_SYS** rail, tapped from protected VBUS (after F1) before FB1 with
  its own polyfuse **F2**, TVS **D3**, 100 uF/16 V + 0.1 uF bulk and an ERC PWR_FLAG,
  so a 5 V-side fault is cleared on the 5 V branch (with the coordination caveat in
  POWER.md - F1/F2 are identical PPTCs, selective tripping is not guaranteed).
* 12 x per-slot 2:1 power mux (**U6..U17**, TPS2111APWR): IN1 = 5V_SYS, IN2 = +3.3 V,
  OUT = the slot rail feeding all five pins of the existing `VSUPPLY_n` socket
  (net `VSLOT_n`). Manual mode, reverse/cross-conduction blocking, adjustable current
  limit (R_ILIM = 1.6 k -> ~312 mA extrapolated, OUTSIDE the datasheet-guaranteed
  range - see POWER.md, needs sign-off).
* Per-slot selection: `SEL_n` with a 100 k pulldown and a 1x02 low-profile header
  (**J7..J18**, 2.00 mm, hidden under a mated module). Shunt fitted = 5V_SYS,
  shunt absent/lost = +3.3 V (fail-safe).
* Per-mux decoupling 1 uF + 0.1 uF on the slot rail; TVS + bulk caps on 5V_SYS.
* `LCSC`/`MPN`/`Manufacturer` fields added to every symbol; BOM values fixed
  (the 24 slot sockets were valued `Conn_02x05_Socket` although they are 1x05;
  simulation sources V1..V3 are no longer offered for assembly) and
  `production/bom.csv` regenerated.
* No LED is added for 5 V indication (module firmware indicates its own rail).
* U5/FB1/FB2 and the 3.3 V rail are unchanged. PCB placement/routing is NOT part of
  this revision - see POWER.md for the Phase 2 constraints.

## 1.2.0
Introduce a new LDO (AP2112K-3.3) which has an EN functionality.
So, we can implement the reset button without using additional components.

Due the older design with a transitor, it won't be able to load mutiple MCUs.

## 1.1.0
Change the push button to a better one.

## 1.0.0
Release 1.0.0

## 0.8.0
Update a footprint of a resistor, so we use the JLCPCB default parts.

## 0.7.0
Add input grounding & remove line_out input buffering

## 0.6.0
Introduce headphone and line out into the base

## 0.5.0

Introduce a RESET button.
Add large capacitors to handle more power fluctuations.

## 0.4.0
Removed power extension via TRS cables. Even with the regulator it will be noisy.
Now we only support GND syncing via TRS.

## 0.3.1

Update the USB-C socket's copper layer masks for proper soldering.

## 0.3.0
Add USB power support to the base.
When connecting multiple base boards, we are sending 5V & the regulator takes care of stepping it down to 3.3v. This will remove some of the critical noise in the setup.


## 0.2.1
Add two Jack sockets each POWER & GND. So, we can cascase if we needed.

## 0.2.0
Add 3.5mm Jack socket for Power & GND delivery between boards.

* Power: Share both 5V & GND between two boards.
* GND: Share only GND between boards

## 0.1.0
Initial Release
